From 858bf0d5c245a3190cc97ab9726e2cd1f03eda95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Tell the desks a changed outcome and show a reopened desk
 its last roll

Flourish and Bending Spoons now send roll_outcome {character_id, action,
outcome, by} to the roller and, unless the roll was secret, the rest of
the table (#19). Each character's last shown roll is kept in memory
(_shown_roll) with its kept die and current outcome; a desk that opens is
sent it as roll_result marked replayed, settled when the table moved
past it, with the post-roll abilities already used (#40). This replaces
roll_settled. The roll is held or remembered before its result goes out,
so a desk opening meanwhile gets the new roll, and a roll sent again with
its id comes back with its current outcome.

Checked: new and flipped tests in test_ws_rolls.py, test_ws_marks.py and
test_surface.py; those files plus the other WebSocket test files pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
